            'Recruiters need to know whether you are in Ankara, Gaziantep, or already in Berlin on a visa. They rarely need the building. A line such as Istanbul, Türkiye, or Kadıköy, Istanbul if you are targeting roles that care about a commute, is enough for almost every private-sector screen. Neighbourhood can help for retail, clinics, and site work. Street, apartment number, and postal code help a courier, not a hiring manager.',
            'Full addresses still appear because older Turkish templates copied the nüfus-style block: name, address, phone, birth date, marital status. That block made sense when a CV was a paper form walked into a personnel office. It is a gift to anyone who collects the file from a job board. If a public institution’s application portal demands a registered address, type it in the portal. Do not print it on the PDF you also upload to a talent pool.',
