            'Read the PDF on your phone in bright light. Check the first screenful: name, title, city, email. That is what a recruiter sees before they scroll. Confirm the active file is this export, not last month’s scan. Confirm language: a mixed TR/EN page looks unfinished unless you did it on purpose for a bilingual desk. Confirm you did not leave Lorem, a placeholder phone, or an internal project name that an NDA covers. Then upload once. Replacing the file five times in an afternoon is how version confusion starts in your own folder.',
            'If the portal rejects the file, believe the error: not PDF, too large, password, or corrupt export. Re-export from the source rather than running the file through three “compress PDF” websites that strip fonts and links. Keep the working source (builder data or a .docx) so you can export again after a typo. The checklist is not a ritual. It is how you stop a 40-minute writing job from failing because the attachment was a picture named cv.pdf.',
